    "created_at": "2026-08-11T22:14:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-11T22:14:22Z",
    "body": "> do you think it makes more sense to add it to the `BluetoothRemoteGATTServer` object?\r\n\r\nYes and no...\r\n\r\nTechnically, I think it needs to be a property of the characteristic because of BlueZ.\r\n\r\nSee discussion in https://github.com/bluez/bluez/issues/199 for BlueZ maintainers reasoning behind that. (As you will see, I didn't really agree with that at the time.)\r\n\r\nThe short version is that it is actually a property of the \"bearer\"/L2CAP channel and the Enhanced Attribute protocol (EATT) allows multiple bearers at the same time. So it would only make sense as a property of the server if the server corresponded to a bearer and we allow multiple server objects in the future.\r\n\r\nIf we want to just stick to the original ATT definition though where there can only be one bearer for ATT per connection, I suppose we could just read that D-Bus property from a random attribute and assume it is the same for all attributes. But that might not always be the case in the future if people start actually making full use of EATT though.\r\n\r\nIn the end, I think having it as a property on the characteristic still makes sense because the `writeWithoutResponse()` method is part of the characteristic object as well. Otherwise, to use it with just a handle to a characteristic object, one would have to write `characteristic.service.device.server.maxWriteWithoutResponseSize` instead of just `characteristic.maxWriteWithoutResponseSize`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
